115-## 7. Deterministic keyword contract
116-
117:The CLI MUST derive seeds before launching any host. Sources, in priority order:
118-
119-1. explicit `relatedDocs` paths and anchors;
120-2. Story title, description, keywords, risk signals, and acceptance wording;
121-3. checklist titles, `userSees`, and `excludes`;
122-4. understanding touchpoints and declared files;
123-5. changed paths, exported symbols, command names, config keys, artifact names, and process-fact names;
124-6. exact identifiers extracted from backticks, flags, JSON keys, environment variables, and error codes;
125-7. bounded memory/playbook hits, labeled advisory and non-authoritative.
126-
127-Each seed records:
128-
129-```ts
--
131-  term: string;
132-  normalizedTerm: string;
133-  sourceType: 'relatedDoc' | 'story' | 'checklist' | 'touchpoint' |
134-    'changedFile' | 'symbol' | 'command' | 'configKey' | 'artifact' |
135-    'processFact' | 'memoryAdvisory';
136-  sourceRef: string;
137-  weight: number;
138-}
139-```
140-
141-Normalization MUST preserve exact identifiers alongside lowercase lexical forms. Hyphen, underscore, slash, camelCase, and acronym variants may be added, but the original token cannot be discarded.
