204-## 9. Local search pipeline
205-
206-### 9.1 Corpus index
207-
208-The CLI builds a deterministic local index containing:
--
214-- optional bounded keyword sketch;
215-- last modified Git commit, when cheap;
216-- document status hints such as execution plan, canonical decision, legacy, or superseded.
217-
218-Complete filename enumeration is mandatory and cheap. Full bodies are not loaded into the routing prompt.
219-
220-### 9.2 Query stages
221-
222-1. Exact path and related-doc match.
223-2. Exact identifier match over filename and headings.
224-3. Exact identifier match over document bodies.
225-4. Normalized lexical match.
226:5. Host-proposed semantic term match.
227-6. Pair queries combining a domain term with a behavior, command, config key, or failure mode.
228-7. Negative-control queries used to detect over-broad terms.
229-
230-Default budgets:
231-
232-- at most 10 `rg` query groups;
233-- at most 50 raw hits per query group;
234:- at most 8 full-read candidates;
235-- at most 2 expansion passes;
236-- zero full-corpus body reads without escalation.
237-
238-The CLI may deduplicate equivalent queries before execution. Deduplication and skipped-query reasons are recorded.
239-
240:## 10. Candidate ranking
241-
242:Candidate score is deterministic after host proposals are collected:
243-
244-```text
245-score =
246-  relatedDocExact          * 100
247-  + changedPathOrSymbol    * 60
248-  + commandOrConfigExact   * 50
249-  + deterministicExactHit  * 35
250-  + headingHit             * 25
251:  + independentHostVotes   * 15
252:  + hostSemanticHit        * 8
253-  + riskDomainMatch        * 10
254-  - legacySuperseded       * 20
255-  - negativeControlNoise   * 15
256-```
257-
258:Weights are versioned constants, not prompt prose. A host cannot directly assign a document score.
259-
260-Tie-breaking order:
261-
262-1. explicit related doc;
263-2. exact identifier or changed-symbol hit;
264-3. number of independent source classes;
265:4. number of independent hosts;
266-5. lexical relative path order.
