310-## 12. Ambiguity and escalation
311-
312-The router MUST escalate instead of guessing when any condition holds:
313-
314-- lifecycle, gate, process-fact, global rename, or cross-cutting policy change;
315-- reviewer explicitly requests escalation;
316-- a relevant filename/title is detected but cannot be safely classified;
317:- score tie crosses the candidate cutoff;
318:- Codex and Claude candidate overlap is below the configured minimum;
319:- a high-confidence host legacy-term proposal has no search result;
320:- top candidates cover fewer than two independent source classes;
321:- a golden known-relevant document falls outside the candidate set;
322-- search results are truncated in a way that could affect ranking;
323-- corpus digest changes after routing;
324-- mechanical read evidence contradicts the declared manifest.
325-
326-`scanEscalationReason` records:
327-
328-- trigger code;
329-- observed ambiguity;
330:- candidate set attempted;
331-- budget already consumed;
332:- requesting host/reviewer;
333-- expanded scope and stop condition.
334-
335-A broad scan is still performed through local tools and read evidence. It is never serialized into a single LLM prompt.
